b6100dbd1583\\\"}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01MnACGiABMMnZcvmM8xoZFU\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"     1→# Guitar Tone Shootout - Development Guide\\\\n     2→\\\\n     3→Code patterns and quality standards.\\\\n     4→\\\\n     5→---\\\\n     6→\\\\n     7→## Quick Start\\\\n     8→\\\\n     9→```bash\\\\n    10→./worktree.py setup main     # First-time: set up main worktree\\\\n    11→./worktree.py setup <issue>  # Create feature worktree from issue\\\\n    12→```\\\\n    13→\\\\n    14→**Idempotent**: Setup works for fresh checkout, existing worktree, or any state in between. Automatically starts services if not running.\\\\n    15→\\\\n    16→**Entry point**: http://localhost:{port} (9000 on main, 9010/9020/etc. on feature worktrees)\\\\n    17→\\\\n    18→---\\\\n    19→\\\\n    20→## How to Run Commands\\\\n    21→\\\\n    22→**Use `just` for ALL commands. Use `just --list` for discovery.**\\\\n    23→\\\\n    24→Commands change over time - always discover dynamically rather than memorising. Before constructing any ad-hoc Docker, uv, or pnpm command, check if `just` already provides it.\\\\n    25→\\\\n    26→**Quick reference:**\\\\n    27→```bash\\\\n    28→just --list           # Find ANY command (ALWAYS check here first)\\\\n    29→just uv-sync          # Sync uv workspace dependencies\\\\n    30→just check            # Quality gates\\\\n    31→just fix-lint         # Auto-fix issues\\\\n    32→just build-astro      # Build Astro frontend\\\\n    33→just verify-astro-sync # Verify dist/ matches src/\\\\n    34→```\\\\n    35→\\\\n    36→**Never guess at commands.** If `just --list` doesn't have it, ask.\\\\n    37→\\\\n    38→---\\\\n    39→\\\\n    40→## Stack\\\\n    41→\\\\n    42→| Layer | Technology |\\\\n    43→|-------|------------|\\\\n    44→| **Package Management** | uv workspaces (monorepo) |\\\\n    45→| **Backend** | FastAPI, SQLAlchemy 2.0, PostgreSQL (dual DB), Redis, TaskIQ, pgmq |\\\\n    46→| **Frontend** | Astro SSG (pre-bundled), Jinja2 SSR, HTMX, Alpine.js, Tailwind |\\\\n    47→| **Testing** | pytest, Playwright |\\\\n    48→| **Quality** | ruff, mypy, import-linter |\\\\n    49→| **Infrastructure** | Docker (db, redis, backend, nginx, worker, scheduler), worktrees |\\\\n    50→\\\\n    51→**Note:** Astro is pre-bundled (`frontend/astro/dist/` committed to git). No Vite dev server at runtime.\\\\n    52→\\\\n    53→---\\\\n    54→\\\\n    55→## Infrastructure Architecture\\\\n    56→\\\\n    57→**Hard separation between build system and runtime.**\\\\n    58→\\\\n    59→| Concern | What It Is | Runtime Reference |\\\\n    60→|---------|------------|-------------------|\\\\n    61→| Build system | Astro, Tailwind, `frontend/astro/` dir | **None** - implementation detail |\\\\n    62→| Static assets | HTML/CSS/JS in `frontend/astro/dist/` | \\\\\\\"static\\\\\\\" or \\\\\\\"assets\\\\\\\" |\\\\n    63→| SSR pages | Jinja2 templates via FastAPI | \\\\\\\"backend\\\\\\\" |\\\\n    64→\\\\n    65→### Dual Database Architecture\\\\n    66→\\\\n    67→| Database | Purpose | Access |\\\\n    68→|----------|---------|--------|\\\\n    69→| `gts_core` | Application data (users, shootouts, chains) | Webapp, worker |\\\\n    70→| `gts_t3k_source` | T3K source data (packs, models, presets) | Worker only |\\\\n    71→\\\\n    72→**Critical**: Webapp has NO direct access to T3K source database. Worker bridges the two databases via pgmq message queues.\\\\n    73→\\\\n    74→### Runtime Stack (ALL environments)\\\\n    75→```\\\\n    76→db, redis, backend, nginx, worker, scheduler\\\\n    77→```\\\\n    78→No astro container at runtime.\\\\n    79→\\\\n    80→### Build-Only Services\\\\n    81→```bash\\\\n    82→# Astro container only starts with --profile build\\\\n    83→docker compose --profile build up astro\\\\n    84→just build-astro        # Starts astro, runs build\\\\n    85→just watch-astro        # Starts astro, watches for changes\\\\n    86→```\\\\n    87→\\\\n    88→### nginx Configuration\\\\n    89→Single `nginx.conf.template` for all environments, processed via envsubst at container startup.\\\\n    90→- Static files served from `/static` (bind-mounted `frontend/astro/dist/`)\\\\n    91→- SSR pages proxied to backend\\\\n    92→- API routes proxied to backend\\\\n    93→\\\\n    94→---\\\\n    95→\\\\n    96→## Development Workflow\\\\n    97→\\\\n    98→```bash\\\\n    99→just uv-sync            # Sync dependencies (after git pull)\\\\n   100→just up-d               # Start services\\\\n\\\\n<system-reminder>\\\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\\\n</system-reminder>\\\\n\\\"}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"01e1fc42-8014-4855-ac0f-4870f8fc20d2\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"d399e1d3-68fe-4c69-b6dd-855df10e79f4\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"file\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/home/ryan/Work/guitar-tone-worktrees/main/AGENTS.md\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"# Guitar Tone Shootout - Development Guide\\\\n\\\\nCode patterns and quality standards.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Quick Start\\\\n\\\\n```bash\\\\n./worktree.py setup main     # First-time: set up main worktree\\\\n./worktree.py setup <issue>  # Create feature worktree from issue\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n**Idempotent**: Setup works for fresh checkout, existing worktree, or any state in between. Automatically starts services if not running.\\\\n\\\\n**Entry point**: http://localhost:{port} (9000 on main, 9010/9020/etc. on feature worktrees)\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## How to Run Commands\\\\n\\\\n**Use `just` for ALL commands. Use `just --list` for discovery.**\\\\n\\\\nCommands change over time - always discover dynamically rather than memorising. Before constructing any ad-hoc Docker, uv, or pnpm command, check if `just` already provides it.\\\\n\\\\n**Quick reference:**\\\\n```bash\\\\njust --list           # Find ANY command (ALWAYS check here first)\\\\njust uv-sync          # Sync uv workspace dependencies\\\\njust check            # Quality gates\\\\njust fix-lint         # Auto-fix issues\\\\njust build-astro      # Build Astro frontend\\\\njust verify-astro-sync # Verify dist/ matches src/\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n**Never guess at commands.** If `just --list` doesn't have it, ask.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Stack\\\\n\\\\n| Layer | Technology |\\\\n|-------|------------|\\\\n| **Package Management** | uv workspaces (monorepo) |\\\\n| **Backend** | FastAPI, SQLAlchemy 2.0, PostgreSQL (dual DB), Redis, TaskIQ, pgmq |\\\\n| **Frontend** | Astro SSG (pre-bundled), Jinja2 SSR, HTMX, Alpine.js, Tailwind |\\\\n| **Testing** | pytest, Playwright |\\\\n| **Quality** | ruff, mypy, import-linter |\\\\n| **Infrastructure** | Docker (db, redis, backend, nginx, worker, scheduler), worktrees |\\\\n\\\\n**Note:** Astro is pre-bundled (`frontend/astro/dist/` committed to git). No Vite dev server at runtime.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Infrastructure Architecture\\\\n\\\\n**Hard separation between build system and runtime.**\\\\n\\\\n| Concern | What It Is | Runtime Reference |\\\\n|---------|------------|-------------------|\\\\n| Build system | Astro, Tailwind, `frontend/astro/` dir | **None** - implementation detail |\\\\n| Static assets | HTML/CSS/JS in `frontend/astro/dist/` | \\\\\\\"static\\\\\\\" or \\\\\\\"assets\\\\\\\" |\\\\n| SSR pages | Jinja2 templates via FastAPI | \\\\\\\"backend\\\\\\\" |\\\\n\\\\n### Dual Database Architecture\\\\n\\\\n| Database | Purpose | Access |\\\\n|----------|---------|--------|\\\\n| `gts_core` | Application data (users, shootouts, chains) | Webapp, worker |\\\\n| `gts_t3k_source` | T3K source data (packs, models, presets) | Worker only |\\\\n\\\\n**Critical**: Webapp has NO direct access to T3K source database. Worker bridges the two databases via pgmq message queues.\\\\n\\\\n### Runtime Stack (ALL environments)\\\\n```\\\\ndb, redis, backend, nginx, worker, scheduler\\\\n```\\\\nNo astro container at runtime.\\\\n\\\\n### Build-Only Services\\\\n```bash\\\\n# Astro container only starts with --profile build\\\\ndocker compose --profile build up astro\\\\njust build-astro        # Starts astro, runs build\\\\njust watch-astro        # Starts astro, watches for changes\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### nginx Configuration\\\\nSingle `nginx.conf.template` for all environments, processed via envsubst at container startup.\\\\n- Static files served from `/static` (bind-mounted `frontend/astro/dist/`)\\\\n- SSR pages proxied to backend\\\\n- API routes proxied to backend\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Development Workflow\\\\n\\\\n```bash\\\\njust uv-sync            # Sync dependencies (after git pull)\\\\njust up-d               # Start services\\\",\\\"numLines\\\":100,\\\"startLine\\\":1,\\\"totalLines\\\":656}}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_01TBcYATobU1sV4xcaskXqMD\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Good. Now let me read the story details for STORY-007:\\\"}],\\\"stop_reason\\\":null,\\\"stop_sequence\\\":null,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":1507,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":82672,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":1507},\\\"output_tokens\\\":1,\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\"},\\\"context_management\\\":null},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"01e1fc42-8014-4855-ac0f-4870f8fc20d2\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"d2c4b72d-e604-4940-8ff9-49f4db482e32\\\"}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"model\\\":\\\"cl